WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Everything starts with your words, kept exactly as you wrote them.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
plumb writes the records first: the intent, requirements with examples, and the decisions.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.000
A judge reads them in the background, so the agent never waits on a model.

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.000
If only you can settle something, you get one plain question, grouped by principle.

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Each example is tied to a test, so passing tests means the examples you agreed to hold.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.000
A merge is checked quickly when git records it, and fully when you push.

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Recap: records first, a background judge, tests tied to examples, and two checks before it lands.

